── NOTCH BOOK (#324): the book each one-notch reopen would buy (cleared + that notch's cohort), every name equal-weight, held 20y ──
  cleared    n=557    book +13.2%/yr  excess +5.8  win 88%  worst -3.3  OOS +4.3/+7.2  top10 +4.3/-3.3
  (n = samples: the cleared book's own, or what the notch adds. `excess`/`bar` are the UNCAPPED book — every admit bought at full weight — kept for continuity with (#324)..(#329). (#330): THE `ship` VERDICT DECIDES AND IT IS READ AT top10 (excess/worst, and the cleared row is the baseline it is measured against), the basket the journaled verdict publishes, where a cohort name must OUTRANK an incumbent to be bought: excess >= that column's `bar`, the p95 of 200 same-n cohorts drawn at random from the refused pool, cutoff-matched and entered at the cohort's own ranks, AND worst >= cleared -1.0, at 20y, 12y and 8y. `inert` = the cohort never reaches the published basket, so the notch changes nothing the tool prints — not a pass, and not a cost it was charged for through (#329). `bar n/a` = the null could not match the cohort's shape, so the row falls back to (#324)'s flat -0.1. `track` grades the same cohorts forward)

